@@ -0,0 +1,133 @@
+# Deploy: TipJar on Base + static site on IPFS
+
+The production site is a static export (`output: "export"`) that talks to **real Base (8453)**. The switch is
+`NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true` (see `packages/nextjs/next.config.ts` and `scaffold.config.ts`). Local dev keeps
+targeting the Base fork (31337, see README.md).
+
+The IPFS build refuses to start unless:
+
+- `deployedContracts.ts` has a `TipJar` entry for chain `8453` (step 1), and
+- `NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL` is set to an `https://` origin (used for Open Graph URLs and images).
+
+Placeholders below: `<production-domain>` (e.g. `tipjar.eth.limo` or your custom domain), `<cid>`, `<gateway>`
+(e.g. `community.bgipfs.com`), `<tipjar-address>`.
+
+Requirements: Node >= 22.4, `yarn install`, Foundry.
+
+## 1. Deploy TipJar to Base (real network, costs gas)
+
+```bash
+yarn generate                    # or: yarn account:import  (creates an encrypted keystore)
+yarn account                     # shows the deployer address; send it a little ETH on Base
+yarn deploy --network base       # deployer becomes the TipJar owner
+yarn verify --network base       # needs ETHERSCAN_API_KEY (Etherscan v2 key) in packages/foundry/.env
+```
+
+Check the deployment and commit the generated `deployedContracts.ts`:
+
+```bash
+grep -n "8453" packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts
+cast call <tipjar-address> "usdc()(address)" --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org    # expect 0x8335...2913
+cast call <tipjar-address> "owner()(address)" --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org   # expect the deployer
+```
+
+## 2. Build
+
+```bash
+cd packages/nextjs
+NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL="https://<production-domain>" \
+  NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY="<your-alchemy-key>" \
+  NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID="<your-walletconnect-project-id>" \
+  yarn build:ipfs
+```
+
+`yarn build:ipfs` deletes `.next` and `out`, then runs `next build` with `NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true` and
+`NODE_OPTIONS=--no-experimental-webstorage` (on Node 25 the half-implemented `localStorage` global otherwise
+crashes the prerender). Use your own Alchemy / WalletConnect keys: the defaults are shared and rate limited, and
+the tip feed reads event logs through that RPC.
+
+## 3. Verify the build before uploading
+
+Run from `packages/nextjs`:
+
+```bash
+ls out/index.html out/*/index.html                       # one index.html per route: debug/, blockexplorer/, 404/ ...
+grep -o '<meta property="og:[a-z:]*" content="[^"]*"' out/index.html   # og:image must start with https://<production-domain>
+grep -c "localhost" out/index.html out/debug/index.html  # expect 0 for both
+grep -rl -i "<tipjar-address>" out/_next/static/chunks   # the Base TipJar address is in the bundle
+grep -rl "USDC Tip Jar" out/index.html                   # the tip jar page, not the SE-2 welcome page
+
+python3 -m http.server 8080 --directory out &            # serve the export locally
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" http://localhost:8080/          # 200
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" http://localhost:8080/debug/    # 200
+kill %1
+```
+
+Open http://localhost:8080 with a wallet on Base: the header must show "Base", the feed must load (empty is fine
+for a fresh contract) and the "In jar" badge must show the real balance.
+
+Optional, with [kubo](https://docs.ipfs.tech/install/command-line/) installed: compute the CID without uploading,
+to compare with what the upload reports.
+
+```bash
+ipfs add -r -Q --only-hash --cid-version 1 out
+```
+
+## 4. Upload
+
+With BuidlGuidl IPFS (bundled as a dev dependency):
+
+```bash
+yarn bgipfs upload config init -u https://upload.bgipfs.com   # add -k <api-key> if you have one
+yarn bgipfs upload out                                        # prints "CID: <cid>"
+```
+
+Or with your own kubo node / pinning service:
+
+```bash
+ipfs add -r -Q --cid-version 1 out     # prints <cid>
+ipfs pin add <cid>                     # or pin <cid> with your pinning service
+```
+
+Do not use `yarn ipfs` for releases: it chains build + upload and skips step 3.
+
+## 5. Post-deploy verification
+
+1. **Record the CID** (release notes / PR). If the CID did not change from the previous release, the uploaded bytes
+   are identical: check the build output and upload target before blaming gateway caching.
+2. **Root and a non-home route through a public gateway** (root success does not prove exported routes resolve):
+
+   ```bash
+   curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "https://<gateway>/ipfs/<cid>/"          # 200
+   curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "https://<gateway>/ipfs/<cid>/debug/"    # 200, not 404
+   curl -s -L "https://<gateway>/ipfs/<cid>/" | grep -o "USDC Tip Jar" | head -1
+   ```
+
+3. **Open Graph uses the production origin**:
+
+   ```bash
+   curl -s -L "https://<gateway>/ipfs/<cid>/" | grep -o '<meta property="og:image" content="[^"]*"'
+   # expect content="https://<production-domain>/thumbnail.jpg"
+   curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" "https://<production-domain>/thumbnail.jpg"   # 200 once the domain serves <cid>
+   ```
+
+4. **App works against Base**: open `https://<gateway>/ipfs/<cid>/`, connect a wallet on Base, send a small tip
+   (e.g. 0.01 USDC), and confirm it appears in the feed and on Basescan:
+
+   ```bash
+   cast call 0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913 "balanceOf(address)(uint256)" <tipjar-address> \
+     --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org
+   ```
+
+5. **ENS (if used)**: set the content hash to `ipfs://<cid>` only after the CID has been reviewed and approved.
+   Then confirm the resolver and the public gateway serve that CID:
+
+   ```bash
+   RPC=https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com
+   NODE=$(cast namehash <name>.eth)
+   RESOLVER=$(cast call 0x00000000000C2E074eC69A0dFb2997BA6C7d2e1e "resolver(bytes32)(address)" $NODE --rpc-url $RPC)
+   cast call $RESOLVER "contenthash(bytes32)(bytes)" $NODE --rpc-url $RPC   # must encode ipfs://<cid>
+   curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "https://<name>.eth.limo/debug/"   # 200
+   ```
+
+The release is done only when all checks above pass.
